{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2c5a4bb56f1348950c2f8fe10bc20b679ce23821e6f65b0d82ef20c4fddcedcc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent is not a sandbox: before running the user's shell it applies a lexical denylist (e.g. `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard`, shutdown commands); other commands and file operations run with the process's own permissions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_476350f166687f7b70dff4932bf3d832b541dcf75ce08797e7620e1c21d693b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product provides one-shot prompts, an interactive terminal UI, local coding tools, durable conversations, and automatic context compaction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_55199b7ae7bf7b3dc8ef0f368410b4187016dc07503fcc734137ea9c8df8bf7b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users sign in with `microcodex login` (a `--device-auth` option exists for remote or headless machines) and can run interactively or pass a one-shot prompt as an argument."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6d2a08efa679accbe146a3243a301e0f555d07b72559ea8478ee75038ac8f9c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is via a curl-piped install script (with `MICROCODEX_RELEASE` selecting a specific release) or by downloading a platform archive from GitHub Releases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_814b5eff35a095df5a6df22fcac21d114de019fe310cabc542827004c887126b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OAuth credentials from login are stored under `$CODEX_HOME`, or `~/.codex` when that variable is unset."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a80d3c7460f983b1f820ed26f27f962f064c2f8c11f4218fc7c8687b5ed4a81c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills are discovered under `$CODEX_HOME/skills` (default `~/.codex/skills`); each needs a `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter name and description, and the full skill is read only when its metadata matches the task."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d639afff502118d2d83cba42a52c2925f46745400f888d15e7de03211be245a1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Linux requires the libcurl and OpenSSL runtime libraries, and prebuilt binaries are published for macOS and Linux on arm64 and x86_64."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d783119fdc45814c405ba90a1796dc801ee3dcc358ade78e035eff3bafdf1d24"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MicroCodex is described as an ultra-lightweight coding agent that runs locally in the terminal and is written in C++23."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f6c9da148f3d567b09251d5165f15d2c3809c54f9073e0e310a869a28ccc225e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented known issues include unimplemented MCP support, inability to copy text from the terminal during use, and a bash safety gate that may miss indirect or unrecognized destructive commands."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2c5a4bb56f1348950c2f8fe10bc20b679ce23821e6f65b0d82ef20c4fddcedcc","clm_476350f166687f7b70dff4932bf3d832b541dcf75ce08797e7620e1c21d693b1","clm_55199b7ae7bf7b3dc8ef0f368410b4187016dc07503fcc734137ea9c8df8bf7b","clm_6d2a08efa679accbe146a3243a301e0f555d07b72559ea8478ee75038ac8f9c4","clm_814b5eff35a095df5a6df22fcac21d114de019fe310cabc542827004c887126b","clm_a80d3c7460f983b1f820ed26f27f962f064c2f8c11f4218fc7c8687b5ed4a81c","clm_d639afff502118d2d83cba42a52c2925f46745400f888d15e7de03211be245a1","clm_d783119fdc45814c405ba90a1796dc801ee3dcc358ade78e035eff3bafdf1d24","clm_f6c9da148f3d567b09251d5165f15d2c3809c54f9073e0e310a869a28ccc225e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:28:51Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7d19db50e414665b59288addef520dc","id":"pg_2a4c29b97ee15d94af3b6d091cae9e8d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/paoloanzn-microcodex-readme-md-2d88e4f57552-6d091cae9e8d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_49444f9139f952da91f5c98fc1682d84"],"title":"paoloanzn/microcodex/README.md @ 2d88e4f57552","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:28:51Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7d19db50e414665b59288addef520dc"}
